You can use LogIt without an account: everything stays on your phone. A free account backs up your phone,
lets you follow people and have a coach; Pro adds sync between phones and the web dashboard.

## Sign in or create an account

On the phone, open Settings and choose Log in. On the web, go to app.getlogit.app.

## Change your plan

In the Android app, open Settings and use the plan card under Account. Pick Pro or Studio, monthly or
yearly; Google Play takes the payment. The web dashboard's Upgrade page explains the plans but can't take
payment. See [What each plan can do](/docs/plans).

## Move to another server

On the phone, **Settings › Move to another server** copies your workouts, splits, nutrition, habits
and settings to another server: from getlogit.app to your own, or back. Make a new account there or
sign in to one you have; if the server is invite-only you'll be asked for the code. The phone only
switches once everything has been copied, so if the copy stops nothing changes and you can try
again. Your old account is kept until you delete it, and social posts and followers stay on the old
server. If you had Pro and move to your own server, cancel Pro in Google Play.

## What a server's admins can see

Whoever runs a LogIt server has an admin console: LogIt does for getlogit.app, and on a server you
host yourself, you and anyone you make an admin do. In it, admins can see your name, username and
email, when you joined, which devices you're signed in on and when you were last around, your plan,
how many posts you have, and posts or comments someone reported. On getlogit.app they also see
where you bought your plan, and any diagnostics log you chose to send from the app.

The console doesn't show your workouts, plans, nutrition, body weight, habits or messages, and
admins can't sign in as you. They can reset your password, sign you out, change your email or plan,
or delete your account. Each change is recorded with who made it, and you get an email about it
when the server has email set up.

Whoever runs a server can still read its database directly. If that matters to you, run your own:
see [Move to another server](#move-to-another-server).

## Delete your account

On the web, open Account (the card at the bottom of the sidebar) and choose Delete account. You'll be
asked for your password. Everything stored on the server goes, including your posts and, for coaches,
any sample clients. What's on your phone stays on your phone.

